How to use them in OpenHands Cloud
Go to https://app.all-hands.dev and sign in.
Start a new conversation.
When choosing a repository, select open-code-cloud-platform-settings.
In your first message, include a trigger phrase for the skill you want.
That's it. The skill loads automatically and shapes the agent's behavior for that conversation.

Example prompts to paste
Planning:

Plan this out before you code: I want to add a nightly job that runs our
test suite and posts a coverage summary.
Security review:

Review the latest commit for security issues. Focus on secrets and
injection.
Coverage:

Run coverage and tell me the lowest-covered modules and what to test next.
Incident triage:

Triage this incident. Here's the error log:
<paste log or stack trace>
Verify it works
Start a conversation on that repo and send just plan this out. If the skill loaded, the agent will respond with a structured plan (Goal, Constraints, Approaches, Steps) instead of jumping to code. That confirms the setup end to end.

Optional add-ons (skip unless you need them)
Secrets — Settings > Secrets. None of the four skills require a token. Add one only if a skill should call an API.
MCP servers — Customize > MCP Servers. Add Datadog if you want incident-triage to pull live errors.
Manage skills in the UI — Customize > Skills shows what's loaded and lets you add more.
Automate a skill — ask the agent to "create an automation" to run a skill on a schedule, e.g. a weekly coverage report.
Using them outside Cloud
The same skills work locally. Clone the repo and run OpenHands from that directory — .agents/skills/ is picked up automatically. You can also copy the .agents/skills/ folder into any other project to reuse them there.

One caveat
The skills are on main now, so a conversation started on that repo picks them up. If you start a conversation on a different repo, these skills won't be present unless you copy .agents/skills/ into it or add them via Customize > Skills in the Cloud UI.
